    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Independent photographer and artist, born 1954, based in Brookline/Boston, MA. Best known for Crowded Fields: composite sports/crowd images made by shooting thousands of frames on a tripod and selectively layering figures (up to 40 hrs per image in Photoshop). BA in Art, UMass Boston (1993); additional study at School of the MFA Boston and Minneapolis College of Art and Design. Work held in public collections at the Fogg Art Museum, Addison Gallery of American Art, DeCordova Museum, Peabody Essex Museum, and MFA Houston; fellowships from Yaddo and the Polaroid Collection; ASME Award for Photography (2023) and ADC Award for Photography (2023); solo shows include Gallery Kayafas (Boston), Houston Center for Photography, Abigail Ogilvy Gallery, and Cortona on the Move (Italy, 2024); represented by Foto Relevance, Houston. First monograph published by Just an Idea Books (2021). Commercial clients include New York Magazine cover. Work Status: Freelance, site and LinkedIn both indicate self-employed independent practice. Autonomy 5: fully independent artist-photographer, no employer, operates at highest level of self-direction across both commercial and fine art work.",
